course: dictionary
lesson: 5504
title: Same word, different jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word laying is a good example. «A modern laying hen can lay about 300 eggs a year» uses laying to mean a hen that makes eggs. The eggs are the clue.
explain: Laying can also mean putting something down carefully, like laying a book on a table, or laying the table for dinner. Look at the words around it. If there are plates, knives and forks nearby, laying means setting the table. If there are bricks or tiles, it means putting them in place.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «The hen is putting down eggs» works, so laying means making eggs. Lay is the base word, laid is the past form, and laying is the -ing form.
fact: Laying is the -ing form of the verb lay: lay, lays, laid, laying.
fact: Laying means putting something down, usually flat or carefully.
fact: A hen laying eggs is making eggs come out of her body.
fact: Laying a table means putting plates, knives and forks on it.
fact: Laying bricks, tiles or a carpet means putting them in place to build or cover something.
exercise: «A modern laying hen can lay about 300 eggs a year.» In this sentence, what does laying mean? | A hen that is lying down to sleep | *A hen that makes eggs | A hen that is cross | A hen that is putting on a hat
exercise: Mum says, «Please help me with laying the table.» What are you doing? | *Putting plates, knives and forks on the table | Washing the dishes | Lying down on the table | Cutting up the food
exercise: Four hens are laying eggs. Each hen lays one egg a day. How many eggs do the hens lay in 3 days? | *12 | 6 | 4 | 7
test: «Farmer Ali is laying bricks to build a wall.» What is laying? | Throwing bricks away | Painting bricks red | *Putting bricks in place | Breaking bricks into pieces
test: Which word is the past form of lay? | laying | *laid | lazy | lays
exam: In science, which animals lay eggs? | Only cows | Only horses | *Birds, reptiles, fish and insects | Only cats and dogs
